name issue_24_timing_v2_default
describe issue_53_cwnd_pushback's link with the default video receive timing: libwebrtc's (timing v2) is the default, so late frames are rendered, not dropped (issue #24)
duration 25s
at 0s  capacity=2500kbps delay=30ms queue=100ms
at 8s  capacity=500kbps
# No `timing` line: this scenario runs the default. It is
# issue_24_timing_v2_render_fps without its `timing v2` line, so it fails
# while the default is timing v1 (FrameScheduler's 10 ms late-drop rule).
# Seeds 1-10: timing v1 16.0-20.8 fps; timing v2 28.8-29.2; libwebrtc on
# issue_53_cwnd_pushback 27.1-27.6 (mean 27.4, parity-data main).
# PR #324 (#84's flip, quality scaling on): was >= 28. Owner sign-off 2026-10-24: ours 27.56 on seed 1, libwebrtc worst seed 1-10 27.52 (mean 27.57).
expect video.render_fps >= 27.5
expect video.residual_loss_pct <= 1.0
# Freezes: timing v1 2806-5621 ms, timing v2 1616-3793, libwebrtc 1816-3617.
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 5000
